    {
      "id": "A01",
      "label": "tax amount at an exact half cent: 1 x 0.25 x 50 % = 0.125 -> 0.13 (half away from zero; banker's rounding and truncation give 0.12)",
      "traps": [
        "numeric-rounding"
      ],
      "reasoning": "TaxAmount = ROUND(PickedQuantity * UnitPrice * TaxRate / 100.0, 2). 1 * 0.25 * 50.000 / 100.0 is exactly 0.125 and the digit before the 5 is even, so half-away-from-zero gives 0.13 while round-half-to-even and truncation both give 0.12. UnitPrice 0.25 ends in 5. ExtendedPrice must be the sum of the two rounded parts.",
