    {
      "id": "A03",
      "label": "an empty DeliveryAddressLine1 with a line 2 gives ', Back door'; a NULL line 2 on the other customer makes its instructions NULL",
      "traps": [
        "null-vs-empty"
      ],
      "reasoning": "DeliveryInstructions = c.DeliveryAddressLine1 + N', ' + c.DeliveryAddressLine2. Customer 1 has line 1 '' and line 2 'Back door', so SQL Server stores ', Back door'; a conversion that turned the empty line 1 into NULL (NULLIF, or a client mapping '' to NULL) would store NULL. Customer 2 has line 2 NULL, so its whole concatenation is NULL with + (and with ||), where concat() would give 'Unit 5, '.",
